# CS4440 Project 1 - Concurrency via Unix Processes and Threads

This project incrementally builds systems programming skills in C using Unix process control and threading, starting from file I/O up to multi-process and multi-threaded concurrency.

What each part teaches:
- System Calls: robust file I/O with open/read/write/close, error handling.
- Parsing & Encoding: run-length compression of long runs (>=16) using tokens -N- (zeros) and +N+ (ones).
- Decompression: token parsing and expansion with careful edge-case handling.
- fork/exec/wait: process creation and program replacement; parent-child synchronization.
- pipe/dup2: IPC and I/O redirection.
- Concurrency: partitioning work across processes/threads and assembling results.
- Mini Shell: command parsing and execution, arguments, and pipelines.

Build (on macOS/Linux):
- Prerequisites: a C toolchain (clang or gcc) and make.
- In this directory, run:

```
make
```

This produces:
- `MyCompress`, `MyDecompress`, `ForkCompress`

Output location:
- All programs write outputs to `project_1/outputs/` using the basename of the destination you pass.
- Example: `./MyCompress input.txt compressed.txt` writes to `outputs/compressed.txt`.

Run examples:
```
# Compress a file of '0'/'1' characters separated by spaces/newlines
./MyCompress input_bits.txt compressed.txt   # creates outputs/compressed.txt

# Decompress (source is the file inside outputs/)
./MyDecompress outputs/compressed.txt decompressed.txt  # creates outputs/decompressed.txt

# Fork + exec MyCompress
./ForkCompress input_bits.txt compressed_via_fork.txt  # creates outputs/compressed_via_fork.txt
```

Notes:
- Compression rule: sequences with length >= 16 are encoded as tokens: `-N-` for zeros, `+N+` for ones; shorter runs are copied as-is. Separators (space/newline) are preserved.
- Decompress expands those tokens back to bits and passes through other characters.
- Use large files to measure timings for parts (10) later.

Cleaning:
```
make clean
```

Testing correctness:
- After compress+decompress, `diff` the original and decompressed files. They should match.

```
./MyCompress big_input.txt big_compressed.txt
./MyDecompress outputs/big_compressed.txt big_out.txt
diff -u big_input.txt outputs/big_out.txt
```
